So that's a reason to be a bit skeptical of this.

266
00:10:39,780 --> 00:10:42,640
All right, now, other experiments find

267
00:10:42,640 --> 00:10:44,200
an even stronger effect and this is the stuff

268
00:10:44,200 --> 00:10:46,800
that I find very interesting and also there have been,

269
00:10:46,800 --> 00:10:48,760
there have been multiple confirmations of this recently.

270
00:10:48,760 --> 00:10:51,120
So it's on pretty solid ground,

271
00:10:51,120 --> 00:10:54,080
which is that at least for some kinds of bipolar disease,

272
00:10:54,080 --> 00:10:54,920
once people believe them,

273
00:10:54,920 --> 00:10:57,200
they tend to grow increasingly confident.

274
00:10:57,200 --> 00:10:58,040
And why?

275
00:10:58,040 --> 00:10:59,640
Well, because they're very likely to notice

276
00:10:59,640 --> 00:11:02,800
anything confirming the initial evidence.

277
00:11:02,800 --> 00:11:04,640
And if you give them some ambiguous evidence,

278
00:11:04,640 --> 00:11:07,920
then they tend to misinterpret it as further support.

279
00:11:07,920 --> 00:11:09,040
And this is a special name,

280
00:11:09,040 --> 00:11:10,740
it is known as confirmatory bias.

281
00:11:16,040 --> 00:11:17,920
Or also confirmation bias.

282
00:11:17,920 --> 00:11:21,000
So you believe a theory and then you look around the world

283
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:23,160
and say, my God, my theory is so confirmed.

284
00:11:23,160 --> 00:11:24,760
Everywhere I look, I see proof.

285
00:11:25,720 --> 00:11:29,120
Right, and the standard common sense reply to this

286
00:11:29,120 --> 00:11:31,960
is you say, look, I see so many pieces of evidence

287
00:11:31,960 --> 00:11:34,640
in favor of my theory, so it's gotta be true.

288
00:11:34,640 --> 00:11:39,640
It's like, well, did you look for evidence

289
00:11:39,680 --> 00:11:42,800
that your theory is wrong?

290
00:11:42,800 --> 00:11:46,400
And then you might find a whole lot of examples of that.

291
00:11:46,400 --> 00:11:47,920
Right, like if I reside a theory

292
00:11:47,920 --> 00:11:49,520
that all men have short hair.

293
00:11:49,520 --> 00:11:50,360
I just look around and say, my God,

294
00:11:50,360 --> 00:11:51,240
I see a whole bunch of theory,

295
00:11:51,240 --> 00:11:53,080
well, like confirmation everywhere.

296
00:11:53,080 --> 00:11:54,560
It's like, well, why don't you look for cases

297
00:11:54,560 --> 00:11:55,600
that are, where that's not true?

298
00:11:55,600 --> 00:11:56,760
A man with long hair.

299
00:11:56,760 --> 00:12:00,320
And then you know, oh, hmm, all right.

300
00:12:00,320 --> 00:12:03,280
But once you've got a theory, it's your theory,

301
00:12:03,280 --> 00:12:06,160
then you start looking around for, let's work with this.

302
00:12:06,160 --> 00:12:08,680
All right, so there is a great experiment

303
00:12:08,680 --> 00:12:11,160
involving the death penalty.

304
00:12:11,160 --> 00:12:12,580
Here's the design.

305
00:12:12,580 --> 00:12:15,840
Step one, we find out who favors the death penalty

306
00:12:15,840 --> 00:12:17,320
and who opposes it.

307
00:12:17,320 --> 00:12:21,580
All right, great, so now, so this begins with actual views,

308
00:12:21,580 --> 00:12:23,480
your actual position on the death penalty.

309
00:12:23,480 --> 00:12:25,440
All right, then we randomly assign people

310
00:12:25,440 --> 00:12:27,160
to two different rooms.

311
00:12:27,160 --> 00:12:31,320
In room one, you are shown cross-sectional studies

312
00:12:31,320 --> 00:12:33,360
that support the death penalty's deterrent effect

313
00:12:33,360 --> 00:12:38,360
and time series that deny the death penalty's deterrent effect

314
00:12:38,360 --> 00:12:41,200
In room two, you do the opposite.

315
00:12:41,200 --> 00:12:43,640
In room two, the time series supports the death penalty

316
00:12:43,640 --> 00:12:46,260
and the cross-section goes against it.

317
00:12:46,260 --> 00:12:48,600
And what do you find occurs

318
00:12:48,600 --> 00:12:51,840
to the confidence of all four groups?

319
00:12:51,840 --> 00:12:56,120
They stick with, worse, they all claim vindication.

320
00:12:56,120 --> 00:12:57,760
And how do you claim, how do the people

321
00:12:57,760 --> 00:12:59,400
in all the rooms claim vindication?

322
00:12:59,400 --> 00:13:02,280
Well, if the cross-sectional evidence is for you

323
00:13:02,280 --> 00:13:04,560
and the time series evidence is against you,

324
00:13:04,560 --> 00:13:07,560
it's just time for a little methodological reflection.

325
00:13:08,400 --> 00:13:10,960
What kind of evidence is the good evidence?

326
00:13:10,960 --> 00:13:11,840
The cross-sectional.

327
00:13:11,840 --> 00:13:13,960
Yeah, whatever supports you is the good evidence.

328
00:13:13,960 --> 00:13:16,840
What kind of evidence is totally meaningless,

329
00:13:16,840 --> 00:13:19,200
irrelevant, debatable?

330
00:13:19,200 --> 00:13:20,920
Yeah, government goes against you.

331
00:13:20,920 --> 00:13:22,840
Right now, of course, if this were not an experimental

332
00:13:22,840 --> 00:13:24,320
design, you could sit around debating

333
00:13:24,320 --> 00:13:27,320
which kind of evidence actually is better or worse.

334
00:13:27,320 --> 00:13:28,640
But since it's an experimental design,

335
00:13:28,640 --> 00:13:30,960
we can show is that people, in fact,

336
00:13:30,960 --> 00:13:34,080
will interpret whatever favors them to be the good method.

337
00:13:34,080 --> 00:13:37,500
So it's a case of abject intellectual corruption,

338
00:13:37,500 --> 00:13:39,920
where you pretend that you are applying

339
00:13:39,920 --> 00:13:41,960
methodological standards, whereas really,

340
00:13:41,960 --> 00:13:44,680
you are just finding out what gives the right answer

341
00:13:44,680 --> 00:13:47,040
and then you are inferring what the good method is

342
00:13:47,040 --> 00:13:50,420
and then using this inference as further support

343
00:13:50,420 --> 00:13:52,000
when in fact, all that you could really,

344
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:53,520
the only honest thing you could say would be,

345
00:13:53,520 --> 00:13:57,400
look, since this is true, then studies that find it are good.

346
00:13:57,400 --> 00:13:59,520
But then, of course, if that's the way you're reasoning,

347
00:13:59,520 --> 00:14:02,320
it's not really additional evidence, is it?

348
00:14:02,320 --> 00:14:03,360
In order to be additional evidence,

349
00:14:03,360 --> 00:14:05,360
it would have to be an amazing framework.

