00:14:46,720 --> 00:14:48,220
and the stock goes down, why?

367
00:14:49,360 --> 00:14:51,760
Why would the price go down when profits are announced?

368
00:14:51,760 --> 00:14:52,640
Not lower than it is.

369
00:14:52,640 --> 00:14:55,160
Yes, because people were expecting better profits,

370
00:14:55,160 --> 00:14:56,200
even more.

371
00:14:56,200 --> 00:14:58,240
Similarly, if the evidence is less supportive

372
00:14:58,240 --> 00:15:01,320
than you were expecting, but still supportive,

373
00:15:01,320 --> 00:15:04,040
this is a reason to actually reduce your confidence.

374
00:15:04,040 --> 00:15:07,300
How many human beings do this for any juicy issue?

375
00:15:08,600 --> 00:15:11,520
Yeah, very, very, maybe not quite none,

376
00:15:11,520 --> 00:15:12,760
but yeah, very few.

377
00:15:13,640 --> 00:15:15,180
It's very rare indeed.

378
00:15:15,180 --> 00:15:16,620
All right, let's see.

379
00:15:16,620 --> 00:15:20,780
And there was a Yale psychologist, Dan Kahan,

380
00:15:20,780 --> 00:15:23,020
who came up and he was actually reporting

